#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:2
msgid "Getting started with |morpheus| and VMware"
msgstr "Getting started con |morpheus| y VMware"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:5
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introducción"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:7
msgid ""
"This guide is designed to help you get started and quickly get the most "
"out of |morpheus| with VMWare. By the end, you will integrate your first "
"cloud, configure networking, prepare and consume images, provision "
"instances, and get started with automation. We will briefly discuss "
"installation and account setup but will provide links to additional "
"resources for those very first steps. For the most part, this guide "
"assumes you are able to get |morpheus| installed and are ready to move "
"forward from that point. There is a lot more to see and do in |morpheus| "
"that is beyond the scope of this guide. For more, consult the complete "
"|morpheus| documentation or take part in our user community forum."
msgstr ""
"This guide is designed to help you get started y quickly get the la "
"mayoría de out of |morpheus| con VMWare. By the end, you will integrate "
"your first cloud, configure networking, prepare y consume images, "
"provision instances, y get started con automation. We will briefly "
"discuss installation y account setup pero will provide links to adicional"
" resources for those very first steps. For the la mayoría de part, this "
"guide assumes you are able to get |morpheus| instalado y are ready to "
"move forward desde that point. There is a lot more to see y do in "
"|morpheus| that is beyond the scope of this guide. For more, consult the "
"complete |morpheus| documentation o take part in our user community "
"forum."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:10
msgid "Installation & Setup"
msgstr "Installation & Setup"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:12
msgid ""
"In the simplest configuration, |morpheus| needs one appliance server "
"which will contain all the components necessary to orchestrate virtual "
"machines and containers. Full requirements, including storage and "
"networking considerations, can be found in |morpheus| documentation `here"
" "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/4.1.0/getting_started/requirements/requirements.html#requirements>`_."
" In order to provision any new instances, hosts, or applications, (or "
"convert any discovered resources to managed resources) you will need a "
"valid license. If you don't have one, you can request a lab license for "
"free at `Morpheus Hub <https://app.morpheushub.com>`_. Once obtained, the"
" license can be applied in |AdmSetLic|."
msgstr ""
"In the simplest configuration, |morpheus| needs one appliance server "
"which will contain all the components necessary to orchestrate máquinas "
"virtuales y containers. Full requirements, including storage y networking"
" considerations, puede ser found in |morpheus| documentation `here "
"<T3>`_. In order aprovisionar any new instances, hosts, o applications,"
" (or convert any discovered resources gestionard resources) you will need"
" a valid license. If you don't have one, you can request a lab license "
"for free at `Morpheus Hub <T4>`_. Once obtained, the license puede ser "
"applied in |AdmSetLic|."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:15
msgid "Groups"
msgstr "Grupos"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:17
msgid ""
"Groups in |morpheus| define which resources a user has access to. Clouds "
"are added to groups and a user can only access clouds that are in the "
"groups to which their roles give them access. More information on "
"|morpheus| groups is `here "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/4.1.1/infrastructure/groups/groups.html#groups>`_."
" A deep dive into groups goes beyond the scope of this guide but it's "
"often useful to create a group that contains all clouds for testing "
"purposes. We will create that group now so that we can add our first "
"cloud into this group in the next section."
msgstr ""
"Groups in |morpheus| define which resources a user has access to. Clouds "
"are added to groups y a user can only access clouds that are en la groups"
" to which their roles give them access. More information on |morpheus| "
"groups is `here "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/4.1.1/infrastructure/groups/groups.html#groups>`_."
" A deep dive into groups goes beyond the scope of this guide but it's "
"often useful to create a group that contains all clouds for testing "
"purposes. We will create that group now so that we can add our first "
"cloud into this group en la next section."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:19
msgid ""
"Navigate to `Infrastructure > Groups`. Here we will see a list of all "
"configured groups but, of course, this will be empty immediately after "
"installation. Click \"+CREATE\". Give your group a name, such as \"All "
"Clouds\". The \"CODE\" field is used when calling |morpheus| through "
"|morpheus| API or |morpheus| CLI. It's useful in most cases to have an "
"\"All Clouds\" group for testing purposes so this will likely help you "
"down the road."
msgstr ""
"Navigate to `Infrastructure > Groups`. Here we will see a list of all "
"configured groups but, of course, this será empty immediately after "
"installation. Click \"+CREATE\". Give your group a name, como \"All "
"Clouds\". The \"CODE\" field is used when calling |morpheus| a través de "
"|morpheus| API o |morpheus| CLI. It's useful in most cases to have an "
"\"All Clouds\" group for testing purposes so this will likely help you "
"down the road."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:21
msgid "The new group dialog box showing a name for the group filled in"
msgstr "The new group dialog box showing a name para la group filled in"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:21
#, fuzzy
msgid ".. image:: /images/vCenterGuideImages/Groups/1groupConfig.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/vCenterGuideImages/Groups/1groupConfig.png"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:26
msgid "Click \"SAVE CHANGES\". Your group is now ready to accept clouds."
msgstr "Click \\\"SAVE CHANGES\\\". Your group is now ready to accept clouds."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:29
msgid "Integrating Your First Cloud"
msgstr "Integrating Your First Cloud"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:31
msgid ""
"Clouds in |morpheus| consist of any consumable endpoint whether that be "
"On-Prem, Public clouds, or even bare metal. In this guide, we will focus "
"on integrating and working with VMWare vCenter."
msgstr ""
"Clouds in |morpheus| consist of any consumable endpoint whether that be "
"On-Prem, Public clouds, o even bare metal. In this guide, we will focus "
"on integrating y working con VMWare vCenter."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:33
msgid ""
"To get started, we will navigate to `Infrastructure > Clouds`. This is "
"the cloud detail page which lists all configured clouds. It will be empty"
" if you've just completed installation and setup of |morpheus| but soon "
"we will see our integrated vCenter cloud here."
msgstr ""
"To get started, we will navigate to `Infrastructure > Clouds`. This is "
"the cloud detail page which lists all configured clouds. It será empty if"
" you've just completed installation y setup of |morpheus| but soon we "
"will see our integrated vCenter cloud here."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:35
msgid ""
"Click the \"+ADD\" button to pop the \"CREATE CLOUD\" wizard. Select "
"\"VMWARE VCENTER\" and click the \"NEXT\" button."
msgstr ""
"Click the \\\"+ADD\\\" button to pop the \\\"CREATE CLOUD\\\" wizard. "
"Select \\\"VMWARE VCENTER\\\" y click the \\\"NEXT\\\" button."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:37
msgid "The list of clouds available to integrate with, vCenter is selected"
msgstr "The list of clouds disponible to integrate with, vCenter is selected"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:37
#, fuzzy
msgid ".. image:: /images/vCenterGuideImages/FirstCloud/1createCloud.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/vCenterGuideImages/FirstCloud/1createCloud.png"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:42
msgid ""
"On the \"CONFIGURE\" tab, we're asked to set the initial connection "
"strings into vSphere. The **API URL** should be in the following format: "
"https://<URL>/sdk. The **USERNAME** should be in user@domain format."
msgstr ""
"On the \\\"CONFIGURE\\\" tab, we're asked establecer the initial "
"connection strings en vSphere. The **API URL** debería ser in lo "
"siguiente format: https://<URL>/sdk. The **USERNAME** debería ser in "
"user@domain format."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:44
msgid "The create cloud dialog box with relevant fields filled"
msgstr "The create cloud dialog box con relevant fields filled"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:44
#, fuzzy
msgid ".. image:: /images/vCenterGuideImages/FirstCloud/2cloudConfigure.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/vCenterGuideImages/FirstCloud/2cloudConfigure.png"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:49
msgid ""
"|morpheus| allows vCenter clouds to be scoped to the **VDC** and "
"**CLUSTER** or even the specific **RESOURCE POOL** if you choose. Once "
"you've entered your URL and credentials, these dropdown menus will become"
" populated."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| allows vCenter clouds to be scoped to the **VDC** y "
"**CLUSTER** o even the específico **RESOURCE POOL** if you choose. Once "
"you've entered your URL y credentials, these dropdown menus serácome "
"populated."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:51
msgid ""
"The **RPC MODE** setting determines how |morpheus| will connect to VMs "
"and make configuration and scripting calls if `Morpheus Agent "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/4.1.1/getting_started/agent/morpheus_agent.html"
"#morpheus-agent>`_ is not installed. In a VMware environment, it is "
"recommended to select **Vmware Tools** but WinRM/SSH are able to be used "
"to configure the guest directly.  If using WinRM, ensure it is configured"
" on the virtual image, discusssed below."
msgstr ""
"The **RPC MODE** setting determines how |morpheus| will connect to VMs y "
"make configuration y scripting calls if `Morpheus Agent <T1>`_ is not "
"installed. In a VMware environment, se recomienda seleccionar **Vmware "
"Tools** but WinRM/SSH are able to be used configurar the guest directly."
"  If using WinRM, ensure it está configurado on the virtual image, "
"discusssed below."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:53
msgid ""
"Additionally, we can opt to **INVENTORY EXISTING INSTANCES** to begin "
"polling VMs for statistics and rightsizing recommendations as well as "
"**ENABLE HYPERVISOR CONSOLE** to use native vSphere console with port 443"
" connectivity between |morpheus| and ESXi hosts."
msgstr ""
"Adicionalmente, we can opt to **INVENTORY EXISTING INSTANCES** to begin "
"polling VMs for statistics y rightsizing recommendations así como "
"**ENABLE HYPERVISOR CONSOLE** to use native vSphere console con port 443 "
"connectivity entre |morpheus| y ESXi hosts."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:55
msgid "To move on, expand the \"Advanced Options\" section."
msgstr "To move on, expand the \\\"Advanced Options\\\" section."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:57
msgid ""
"Within the \"Advanced Options\" drawer are additional configurations to "
"consider for your first cloud. Some of these won't usable until they "
"reference additional configured integrations. Common settings to consider"
" are **DOMAIN**, **STORAGE TYPE**, **APPLIANCE URL** (overrides the "
"|morpheus| URL for external systems), **GUIDANCE** (setting \"Manual\" "
"will make recommendations for rightsizing), and **AGENT INSTALL MODE**."
msgstr ""
"Within the \\\"Advanced Options\\\" drawer are adicional configurations "
"to consider for your first cloud. Some of these won't usable until they "
"reference adicional configurado integrations. Common settings to consider"
" are **DOMAIN**, **STORAGE TYPE**, **APPLIANCE URL** (overrides the "
"|morpheus| URL for externo systems), **GUIDANCE** (setting \\\"Manual\\\""
" will make recommendations for rightsizing), y **AGENT INSTALL MODE**."

