#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:75
msgid ""
"On the final tab of the \"CREATE CLOUD\" wizard, you'll confirm your "
"selections and click \"COMPLETE\". The new cloud is now listed on the "
"cloud detail page. After a short time, |morpheus| will provide summary "
"information and statistics on existing virtual machines, networks, and "
"other resources available in the cloud."
msgstr ""
"On the final tab of the \"CREATE CLOUD\" wizard, you'll confirm your "
"selections y click \"COMPLETE\". The new cloud is now listed on la nube "
"detail page. After a short time, |morpheus| will provide summary "
"information y statistics on existing virtual machines, networks, y other "
"resources available in la nube."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:78
msgid "Viewing Cloud Inventory"
msgstr "Viewing Cloud Inventory"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:80
msgid ""
"Now that we've integrated our first VMware cloud, we can stop for a "
"moment to review what |morpheus| gives us from the cloud detail page. We "
"can see that |morpheus| gives us estimated costs and cost histories, "
"metrics on used resources, and also lists out resource counts in various "
"categories including container hosts, hypervisors, and virtual machines. "
"We can drill into these categories to see lists of resources in the "
"various categories individual resources within them by clicking on the "
"category tabs. We can link to the detail page for any specific resource "
"by clicking on it from its resource category list."
msgstr ""
"Now that we've integrated our first VMware cloud, we can stop for a "
"moment to review what |morpheus| gives us desde la nube detail page. We "
"can see that |morpheus| gives us estimated costs y cost histories, "
"metrics on used resources, y también lists out resource counts in various"
" categories including container hosts, hypervisors, y virtual machines. "
"We can drill en these categories to see lists of resources in the various"
" categories individual resources dentro de them by clicking on the "
"category tabs. We can link to the detail page for cualquier específico "
"resource by clicking on it desde its resource category list."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:83
msgid "Configuring Resource Pools"
msgstr "Configuring Resource Pools"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:85
msgid ""
"With our VMware cloud configured, |morpheus| will automatically sync in "
"available resource pools and data stores."
msgstr ""
"With our VMware cloud configured, |morpheus| will automatically sync in "
"disponible resource pools y data stores."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:87
msgid ""
"For resource pools, once |morpheus| has had time to ingest them, then "
"will be visible from the cloud detail page. Navigate to `Infrastructure >"
" Clouds > (your VMware cloud) > RESOURCES tab`. In here, we are able to "
"see and control access to the various resource pools that have been "
"configured in vCenter. For example, we can restrict access to a specific "
"resource pool within |morpheus| completely by clicking on the \"ACTIONS\""
" button, then clicking \"Edit\". If we unmark the \"ACTIVE\" button and "
"then click \"SAVE CHANGES\" we will see that the resource pool is now "
"grayed out in the list. The resources contained in that pool will not be "
"accessible for provisioning within |morpheus|."
msgstr ""
"For resource pools, once |morpheus| has had time to ingest them, entonces"
" será visible desde la nube detail page. Navigate to `Infrastructure > "
"Clouds > (your VMware cloud) > RESOURCES tab`. In here, we are able to "
"see y control access to the various resource pools that han sido "
"configurados in vCenter. Por ejemplo, we can restrict access to a "
"específico resource pool dentro de |morpheus| completely by clicking on "
"the \"ACTIONS\" button, entonces clicking \"Edit\". If we unmark the "
"\"ACTIVE\" button y entonces click \"SAVE CHANGES\" we will see that the "
"resource pool is now grayed out in the list. The resources contained in "
"that pool no be accessible for provisioning dentro de |morpheus|."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:89
msgid "The list of synced resource pools in |morpheus|"
msgstr "The list of synced resource pools in |morpheus|"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:89
#, fuzzy
msgid ".. image:: /images/vCenterGuideImages/ResourcePools/1resourcePools.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/vCenterGuideImages/ResourcePools/1resourcePools.png"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:94
msgid ""
"Often our clients will want to make specific blocks of resources "
"available to their own customers. This can be easily and conveniently "
"controlled through the same \"EDIT RESOURCE POOL\" dialog box we were "
"just working in. If we expand the \"Group Access\" drawer, we are able to"
" give or remove access to each pool to any group we'd like. We can also "
"choose to make some or all of our resource pools available to every "
"group. Specific resource pools can also be defined as the default for "
"each group if needed."
msgstr ""
"Often our clients will want to make specific blocks of resources "
"available a lair own customers. This puede ser easily y conveniently "
"controlled a través de the same \"EDIT RESOURCE POOL\" dialog box we were"
" just working in. If we expand the \"Group Access\" drawer, we are able "
"to give o remove access to each pool to any group we'd like. We can "
"también choose to make some o all of our resource pools available to "
"every group. Specific resource pools can también be defined as the "
"default for each group si es necesario."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:96
msgid "The edit resource pools dialog box"
msgstr "The edit resource pools dialog box"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:96
#, fuzzy
msgid ".. image:: /images/vCenterGuideImages/ResourcePools/2editResourcePools.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/vCenterGuideImages/ResourcePools/2editResourcePools.png"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:101
msgid ""
"Additionally, we may choose to allow only certain service plans to be "
"provisioned into a specific pool of resources. For example, perhaps a "
"specific cluster is my SQL cluster and only specific services plans "
"should be consumable within it. We can control that through this same "
"dialog box."
msgstr ""
"Adicionalmente, we may choose to allow solo certain service plans to be "
"provisioned en a específico pool of resources. Por ejemplo, perhaps a "
"específico cluster is my SQL cluster y solo específico services plans "
"debería ser consumable dentro de it. We can control that a través de this"
" mismo dialog box."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:104
msgid "Configuring Data Stores"
msgstr "Configuring Data Stores"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:106
msgid ""
"To take a look at data stores, we'll move from the \"RESOURCES\" tab to "
"the \"DATA STORES\" tab on our cloud detail page."
msgstr ""
"To take a look at data stores, we'll move desde the \\\"RESOURCES\\\" tab"
" to the \\\"DATA STORES\\\" tab on our cloud detail page."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:108
msgid ""
"|morpheus| gives the user similar control with data stores to what we saw"
" with our resources pools earlier. Just like with resource pools, we can "
"disable access within |morpheus| completely by clicking on \"ACTIONS\" "
"and then \"Edit\". If we unmark the \"ACTIVE\" checkbox and click \"SAVE "
"CHANGES\", you will see that specific data store has been grayed out."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| gives el usuario similar control con data stores to what we "
"saw con our resources pools earlier. Just like con resource pools, we can"
" disable access dentro de |morpheus| completely by clicking on "
"\"ACTIONS\" y entonces \"Edit\". If we unmark the \"ACTIVE\" checkbox y "
"click \"SAVE CHANGES\", you will see that específico data store ha sido "
"grayed out."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.rst:110
msgid "The list of synced data stored in |morpheus|"
